INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'2d351405-3d1d-4b0e-9e66-0e7bf2cee0e2', N'210c7148-726e-4e8b-bf12-40be36e55130', N'What is the difference between static and dynamic dispatch in Rust?', N'Middle', N'Static dispatch uses generics with trait bounds to generate specialized code for each type at compile-time, which allows for better inlining and optimization. Dynamic dispatch uses trait objects with vtables to resolve method calls at runtime, providing flexibility but incurring a small performance penalty due to pointer indirection.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6fc1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
