INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'a2e91dd7-8b65-4e59-b7c6-6c6392c9b8b7', N'0b90236e-1b84-4abe-abc2-c153ce1b03d9', N'What is the difference between a primary key in SQL and the _id in MongoDB?', N'Intern', N'In SQL, a primary key must be explicitly defined and enforced by the table schema. In MongoDB, the _id field is automatically generated by default if the developer does not provide one, ensuring every document is unique.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6ec1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
