INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'd11d7ceb-7cc5-426d-a994-880d4887f34c', N'ede98781-dbb4-4edd-88de-2db0c39c5f9e', N'Why might you use a ''nested'' data type instead of an ''object'' type for arrays of objects?', N'Middle', N'The object type flattens nested structures, which can lead to cross-object matching issues where query criteria are accidentally satisfied across different items. The nested type indexes each object as a hidden separate document, allowing for independent query and aggregation of individual items.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6ec1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'd7de1fe3-99d1-493a-8c56-88108f5a0922', N'7d778e96-db84-4b18-88a8-dc9859f564ac', N'Why is ''method_missing'' considered a powerful yet risky tool?', N'Middle', N'It allows a class to intercept calls to non-existent methods, enabling dynamic interfaces and metaprogramming. However, it is risky because it can hide bugs by making invalid method calls appear successful, and it negatively impacts performance by bypassing standard method lookup.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6fc1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
