INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'22c2ea34-490d-43cd-8963-944d36bb0a67', N'0b90236e-1b84-4abe-abc2-c153ce1b03d9', N'Describe the function of the oplog in MongoDB replication.', N'Senior', N'The oplog is a capped collection that stores a rolling record of all operations that modify data in the database. Secondaries poll the primary''s oplog and apply these operations sequentially to their own data sets to maintain eventual consistency.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6ec1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
