INSERT [dbo].[Questions] ([QuestionId], [CategoryId], [Question], [Difficulty], [Answer], [Status], [IsDeleted], [DeletedAt], [CreatedBy], [CreatedAt], [UpdatedAt], [DeletedBy], [PositionId]) VALUES (N'f02f5a4e-f90f-42e3-a58a-ebb48bb83f23', N'bb0c1e54-46e9-4a65-98a2-e93a00322228', N'What does a ''deadlock'' mean in the context of PostgreSQL transactions?', N'Middle', N'A deadlock occurs when two or more transactions are waiting for each other to release locks, creating a circular dependency. PostgreSQL automatically detects these situations and aborts one of the involved transactions to break the loop.', N'Active', 0, NULL, NULL, CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.3860866' AS DateTime2), CAST(N'2026-07-13T14:49:57.4119316' AS DateTime2), NULL, N'6ec1cfe6-a888-f111-b9fd-d362599bedcb')
